#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:4
msgid "Deployment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:6
msgid ""
"This page gives complete deployment samples for the two long-running "
"components: a hub (``anet-hub`` with the optional ``anet-hub-admin``) and"
" a node (the ``anet`` daemon). Each is shown as a set of systemd units "
"and as a container image. The samples are starting points; the host "
"names, paths and account names are examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:18
msgid "Principles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:20
msgid ""
"**Dedicated account.** Run each component under its own unprivileged "
"account. The data directory holds private keys and is created with mode "
"``0700``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:23
msgid ""
"**Loopback listeners.** A hub listens on a loopback address and a reverse"
" proxy terminates TLS (see :ref:`ops-hub-proxy`). A node's control plane "
"and local A2A interface are loopback-only and must not be published."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:26
msgid ""
"**Secrets in files.** Tokens are kept in files readable by the service "
"account only and are never placed in a unit file, an image or a command "
"line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:29
msgid ""
"**Write access to the data directory only.** The units below mount the "
"file system read-only and open the data directory for writing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:31
msgid ""
"**One data directory, one process.** Two processes on the same hub data "
"directory, or two copies of one node identity running at the same time, "
"are both faults (see :ref:`ops-backup`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:37
msgid "A hub with systemd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:39
msgid ""
"The installation uses one account, ``anet-hub``, for the hub, the "
"operator plane and the maintenance job. The operator plane writes to the "
"hub's database (to deregister an agent), so it needs the same account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:44
msgid "Account and files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:56
msgid ""
"``deploy/hub-db-roll.sh`` is in the ANetHub repository. It needs the "
"``sqlite3`` command. The data directories are created by systemd from the"
" ``StateDirectory=`` lines of the units below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:61
msgid "Hub unit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:63
msgid "``/etc/systemd/system/anet-hub.service``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:113
msgid "Operator-plane unit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:115
msgid ""
"The operator plane reads the token from ``/etc/anet-hub/admin.env``. "
"systemd reads that file before it drops privileges, so the file can be "
"owned by ``root`` with mode ``0600``. The unit is omitted entirely on a "
"hub that does not use the console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:120
msgid "``/etc/systemd/system/anet-hub-admin.service``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:169
msgid ""
"Without an ``ADMIN_TOKEN`` line in the file, or with a placeholder value,"
" the service does not start. Check a token before restarting the service:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:177
msgid "Maintenance job"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:179
msgid ""
"``hub-db-roll.sh`` checkpoints the write-ahead log, writes the weekly "
"backup and prunes old backups (see :ref:`ops-backup`). It runs once a "
"day."
msgstr ""

