msgid "Start everything"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:237
msgid ""
"Then set the recovery passphrase of the hub identity. The hub must be "
"stopped for this step, and the command must run in a terminal. Choose a "
"recovery-file location outside the data directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:249
msgid ""
"Copy ``hub.anetrec`` to separate storage. Later ``identity status`` and "
"``identity rotate`` commands name the same file with ``--recovery-file``,"
" because the service account has no home directory. Other operator "
"subcommands are run the same way, as the service account:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:258
msgid ""
"Finally publish the hub through the reverse proxy configuration shown in "
":ref:`ops-hub-proxy`, and request the certificate for the host name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:263
msgid "A hub in a container"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:265
msgid ""
"The project does not publish a container image. The following "
"``Containerfile`` builds a minimal one around a static ``anet-hub`` "
"binary (built with ``CGO_ENABLED=0``). The image has no shell; it holds "
"the binary and an empty, writable ``/data`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:282
msgid ""
"Build and start it. The port is published on the loopback interface of "
"the host only, so the reverse proxy remains the single public face:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:296
msgid ""
"Arguments after the image name are appended to the entry point, so "
"``--public-url`` and the other options of :ref:`ops-hub` can be given "
"there. Operator subcommands run in a second container on the same volume."
" Set the recovery passphrase with the hub container stopped, and keep the"
" recovery file on a separate bind mount owned by the image's user (uid "
"65532):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:313
msgid ""
"The hub writes its log to standard error; ``docker logs anet-hub`` shows "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:317
msgid "A node with systemd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:319
msgid ""
"A node that must run without a logged-in user (a provider of public "
"capabilities, for example) is an ``anet daemon`` under its own account. "
"The data directory is ``ANET_DATA_DIR``. The command-line tool refuses to"
" talk to a daemon that runs under another user, so commands for the node "
"are run as its account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:331
msgid "``/etc/systemd/system/anet-node.service``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:385
msgid ""
"``RestrictNamespaces=yes`` and the system-call filter prevent the sandbox"
" of the auto-reply module from starting, because the sandbox creates "
"namespaces. A node that answers tasks with a sandboxed local agent needs "
"these two lines relaxed (see :ref:`topics-sandbox`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:390
msgid ""
"A small wrapper runs the command-line tool as the node's account with the"
" same environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:393
msgid "``/usr/local/bin/anet-node``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:412
msgid ""
"``hub-register`` asks for the recovery passphrase on the terminal and "
"writes the recovery file to ``/var/lib/anet-node/.anet-recovery/``, "
"outside the data directory. Copy that file to separate storage (see :ref"
":`ops-backup`). Without a terminal, registration still completes, and the"
" node reports that the identity has no recovery passphrase until ``anet "
"identity protect`` is run in a terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:424
msgid "A node in a container"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:426
msgid ""
"The same approach works for a node. The image holds a static ``anet`` "
"binary, a writable ``/data`` directory for the node's data and a writable"
" ``/recovery`` directory that receives the recovery file. Keep the two on"
" separate volumes so that they can be backed up and stored separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:454
msgid ""
"The control plane and the local A2A interface listen on the container's "
"own loopback interface and are not published; commands reach them through"
" ``docker exec``. Do not publish those ports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:460
msgid "Checklist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:462
msgid "Before a hub accepts nodes from the Internet:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:464
msgid ""
"``/healthz`` answers through the public name over HTTPS, and the version "
"is the one installed most recently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:466
msgid ""
"The proxy sets ``X-Real-IP``, allows request bodies of at least "
"``--relay-max-envelope``, and keeps no access log."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:468
msgid ""
"The hub identity has a recovery passphrase, and a copy of the recovery "
"file is stored away from the host."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:470
msgid ""
"The operator plane, when used, answers only through the proxy and its "
"token is neither a placeholder nor shared with another system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:472
msgid ""
"The daily maintenance job has run once (``roll.log`` in the data "
"directory) and a backup can be restored on a test host (:ref:`ops-"
"backup`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/deployment.rst:475
msgid ""
"``anet-hub admission`` shows the intended mode, and ``federation.json`` "
"lists exactly the intended peers (:ref:`ops-federation`)."
msgstr ""

